{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vv8FsNegHMxfb2V8MznLn4","type":"tool_result","content":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n279:- `input.box()` †: the pointer's gestures, read each step in screen pixels (the HUD's space), from a mouse or one finger: box() -> { x0, y0, x1, y1, from, to, done } while a box is drawn (a mouse's left button dragged; on a touch screen a long press, then a drag), done the step it is let go; else null\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ...\n288:- `input.drag()` †: how far the touch stick's finger moved since the last step, in screen pixels [dx, dy] (the HUD's space), or null while no finger holds it: to steer one to one (a shooter's ship follows the thumb) instead of by the stick's direction\n289:- `input.feed(type, x, y, o = {})` †: a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false, button: 0, id: 0 (which finger, for zones) }) (a test's or a bot's mouse and fingers: clicks, boxes, long presses, double taps and pans follow; a finger in one of the zones holds its act), or feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n316:- `input.touchArea()` †: where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or null while none show: keep a prompt or a box clear of it (a bottom E.Dialog does by itself)\n317:- `input.touchButtons(actions, o = {})` †: On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide them, put them on the left, and size them): input.touchButtons(['jump', 'attack'], { labels: { jump: 'A', attack: 'B' }, force }). The other half of the screen is a move stick (past halfway it presses up, down, left and right too, as a d-pad does: menus and ladders). START is the corner's menu button, top right: it opens the menu, or pauses a pausable scene into it (without the corner a START button there starts a title and pauses, as a gamepad's Start)\n318:- `input.touchSet(a, label = null, show = true)` †: one touch button as the moment changes: its label (TALK beside someone, NEXT in a dialog; null: its own) and whether it shows (false: nothing for it to do here). Cheap to call every step: input.touchSet('confirm', near ? 'TALK' : null, near || talking)\n179:- `E.rng(s)`: a seeded random stream: const R = E.rng(42); R() gives 0..1, the same numbers for the same seed (mulberry32)\n183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n869:- `level.cells`: stored bottom row first: cz = 0 is the lowest row and z grows upward\n1095:- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes first. An id that is already there warns and keeps the first. Returns { shapes: [ids], materials: [ids], sprites: { id: sprite } } (sprites are E.sprite data; a color may be 'material:tone', tone deep | sh | base | lt | hi)\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n2270:class Game {\n2294:  constructor(o = {}) {\n3944:  constructor(o = {}) {\n4866:  constructor(o = {}) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"1626abdb-9e61-487d-aa0f-6749c6ced22e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:25:49.686Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"55:- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n