{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghbMmgM6Jo9WRNfk4PBB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QesgEgx5mWmP3g1d4Ys4XY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 380,420p hub/README.md | cut -c1-220; grep -n \"connect\\|answer\\|ready(\\|finish(\" vendor/aihub-session.js | head -20 | cut -c1-180","description":"Read the hub events table and find the client method names"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1793,"cache_read_input_tokens":421511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1793},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"b182cd70-c34d-4164-8224-77e4d597c825","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:44:14.561Z","request_id":"req_011CghbMmFZSkhyd7moBRJLb","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QesgEgx5mWmP3g1d4Ys4XY":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-012424__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424 && sed -n 380,420p hub/README.md | cut -c1-220; grep -n \"connect\\|answer\\|ready(\\|finish(\" vendor/aihub-session.js | head -20 | cut -c1-180","description":"Read the hub events table and find the client method names"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01QesgEgx5mWmP3g1d4Ys4XY":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-012424__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QesgEgx5mWmP3g1d4Ys4XY","type":"tool_result","content":"| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n36:    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n162:  var connecting = null;\n248:      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n291:  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n292:    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n297:    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n309:        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n327:  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n328:  hub.answer = function (what) {\n330:    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n331:    post('answer', { answer: what });","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"13a41cbe-faa8-4e4c-889d-b06bc1d6ffcd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:44:14.575Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n36:    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n162:  var connecting = null;\n248:      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n291:  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n292:    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n297:    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n309:        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n327:  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n328:  hub.answer = function (what) {\n330:    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n331:    post('answer', { answer: what });","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QesgEgx5mWmP3g1d4Ys4XY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
