{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcPDT39UszbCfZGeurh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D2XUfAgad2A7VFKAeh9yv5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, engine/my-3d2dge.js)\n\nEvery change in the engine file is marked `AOA:` in a comment so it can be found with `grep -n AOA:`.\n\n## Made\n\n1. **Button symbols default to PlayStation** (`Input` constructor, `this.glyphs`, and the Settings entry \"Button symbols\").\n   The TASK asks for PlayStation glyphs by default, with an Xbox A B X Y option in Settings. The option list now starts with\n   PlayStation, then Xbox. Test: `test/run.mjs`, the ui and prompt checks, and the browser walk (keycap and ✕ glyphs).\n2. **A function dialog voice gets every letter** (`Dialog`'s typing). When `voice` is a function it is called for every newly\n   shown letter `(ch, index, page, dialog)`. Sound presets still work as before. The game's own text box (`src/11b-text.js`)\n   does the voices itself, so this hook is present but not used by the game yet.\n\n## Not made (the plan's patch list, and what the game does instead)\n\n- Patch 1, the PlayStation symbols in the pixel font: not added to the font table. The game maps the symbols it needs to\n  characters the font has (`src/00-core.js`, `G.FONT_SAFE`) and draws the controller glyphs as pixel art (`src/10-input.js`).\n- Patch 4, audio buses and instrument tables: not made. Music uses the engine's own wave types and step notation;\n  sound effects use the engine's presets and custom voices.\n- Patch 5, the athletic build, swimsuit cuts and patterns, extra hair and hat styles, `extras` and new poses: not made.\n  Suits are drawn as outfit colours (top = main, shorts = accent, trim = lines); hair is mapped to the five engine styles;\n  accessories are drawn as small overlays after the rig (`G.drawAccessories`).\n- Patch 6, the session combo rule (`reserveCombo`): not made. The session's Options/Create handling is the engine's default.\n- Patch 7, touch off: done in the game (`G.game.input.touchEnabled = false`), not in the engine.\n- Patch 8, registering the court and serve-cam views: done in the game with `new E.View(...)`, not in `E.VIEWS`.\nEOF\ncat > README-DEV.md <<'EOF'\n# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball: dev notes (built by claude-haiku-5-5, medium effort)\n\nThis folder is the dev folder. The deliverable is one level up:\n`../AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424.html`.\nThe exit interview is `../exit-interview.json` (written by `tools/exit.mjs` from the game's own data, `src/55-about.js`).\n\n## Commands\n- `node tools/build.mjs`: builds `build/game.js`, `build/dev.html` and the deliverable.\n- `node test/run.mjs`: the whole test command. It prints only failures and one count line.\n  Flags: `--only=a,b` (suites: core, data, ball, match, vacation, casino, story, ui, game, poolhop, playthrough, browser, hub),\n  `--skip-browser` (no Chromium), `--skip-hub` (no hub harness).\n- `node tools/browser-check.mjs`: opens the deliverable from file:// and walks the title, Beach Match and the pause menu.\n- `node tools/hub-check.mjs [players] [scenario] [latency jitter loss]`: one AI Hub harness run (scenarios: standard,\n  server, host-leave). Starts and stops its own Python server by PID.\n- `node tools/exit.mjs`: writes `exit-interview.json`.\n\n## Layout (src, concatenated in name order inside one IIFE)\n- 00 core (rng streams, bus, money, the font sanitiser), 01 tuning (G.T sliders), 02 cast, 03 items, 04 world (places, maps,\n  schedules), 05 dialogue, 06 songs, 10 input maps and prompts, 11 UI kit, 11b text box, 12 sound and Animalese voices,\n  13 rigs, 14 beach court, 20 ball (closed form), 21 match class and referee, 22 players and the judge, 23 AI,\n  24 match loop, 25 AI Hub session, 26 match scene and HUD, 27 commentary, hints and the final's specials, 30 vacation rules,\n  31 island map, 32 walkable places, 33 shops, wardrobe, journal, mail, 34 story, 40 Pool Hop, 41 casino, 42 photo and album,\n  50 title and menu, 50b How to Play and About, 51 attract, 52 Beach Match setup, 53 dev panel, 54 day end, endings, credits,\n  results, 55 About data, 99 main (scenes, pause menu, saves, match results routing).\n\n## What is built (and how far)\n- Beach volleyball: 2v2 with one timed Play button (bump, set, spike, serve), shot/block, dive, Mine/Yours calls, aim by stick or\n  mouse, rally scoring, faults, AI partner and opponents with chemistry, a Broadcast camera with a Serve Cam toggle, a HUD,\n  judgement popups, commentary from Sonny, Pepper's tutorial hints, the final's Golden Glare, House Edge and Lucky Seven.\n- Vacation: five days of three slots, weather, moods, schedules and teams, affinity, gifts, team-ups, the Match Board, money,\n  the day end, the story (invitation, character select, arrival, Welcome Match, rain, the overheard call, semifinal, final,\n  party, two endings), saves (three slots and Continue), New Vacation+ (carried-over wardrobe and album).\n- Places: the beach, the pool, the promenade, the villa and the casino floor are walkable TileMaps; the island map is a pin\n  list over a painted island. Shops, wardrobe, journal (friends, stats, save), mailbox, album, photo mode.\n- Pool Hop (beat judge, slips, wobble and double pads), casino (cashier, Fortuna Sevens with stop buttons, blackjack,\n  roulette). Slot return is about 91% (`test`: 89–95%).\n- Audio: nine songs in step notation, about 60 chip-synth effects, Animalese voices per letter for dialogue.\n- Front end: title with the fighters on the sand, main menu, How to Play (ten pages), About & Credits (five pages), attract\n  (one AI match and a title card), dev panel (tools and every tuning slider, reset, copy JSON), touch-only gate.\n- AI Hub shared-world session: four seats, the host runs the match on the hub clock and broadcasts snapshots and launches,\n  clients send presses and move; the harness passes in four scenarios.\n\n## Known gaps (not built, or built more simply than the plan)\n- Swimsuit cuts and patterns, hair and hat styles, motion-capture clips and arm IK: not built (see ENGINE-CHANGES.md).\n- Attract mode: one match and a title card, not the full montage of seven beats.\n- Highlight replays (ring buffer, slow-motion replay): not built.\n- Photo album: postcards are shown as framed cards, not re-rendered scenes. Photo poses are limited to the pose names.\n- Dev panel: tools, vacation actions and tuning; not the Voice Lab, music jukebox, SFX board or rig sheet viewer.\n- Online: the host's presses are applied on arrival (no client-side claims and validation as the plan describes).\n- Beach Match: up to four local players through the engine's join; teams fill in join order.\n- Voices: dialogue only (no barks in matches).\nEOF\nrm -rf .tmp && rm -f tools/smoke.mjs tools/smoke2.mjs && ls && node tools/build.mjs | tail -1","description":"Write engine-change record and dev notes; clear scratch files and rebuild"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":552299,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"596226f5-3fe3-4590-a85f-a74c2577c6a6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:57:56.326Z","request_id":"req_011CghcPCroyateZHHnsUsX2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01D2XUfAgad2A7VFKAeh9yv5":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-012424__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXt