{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghccc3TLrvPQ9uEQM26W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build is complete and all checks pass, but the goal is not fully met. The plan is large, and several features are built in simpler form or not at all. Those gaps are listed below.\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- **Game:** `AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424.html` in the work folder. It is a single 1.5 MB file that opens from `file://` with no external requests.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` in the work folder. It parses and fills every field, and it is written from the same data as the in-game About screen.\n- **Dev folder:** `AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424/`, with `README-DEV.md` and `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n\n**Title and approach.** I used the title from PLAN.md (*Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball*) because TASK.md says to. The plan's folder names, date and model were replaced with the TASK.md ones.\n\n## Verification\n\n`node test/run.mjs` runs 95 checks, all passing, in about 57 seconds. They cover:\n- Physics, data counts and the planned tests for the match, the vacation, the casino and the story.\n- Full AI-only matches over 12 seeds, plus a full human-driven match with a timing bot.\n- Slot return of about 91%, within the planned 89–95% band.\n- A browser check of the deliverable, with no console errors.\n- The AI Hub harness in all four planned scenarios: 4 players under latency, a server copy, the host leaving, and one player.\n\nI did not review every screen visually. I checked the title, the character select, the setup, the match and the invitation.\n\n## Not built or simplified\n\n- **Swimsuits and hair:** suits are outfit colours only. The swimsuit cuts, patterns and extra hair styles need engine patches I did not make.\n- **Animation:** no motion-capture clips and no arm IK. Poses come from the engine's built-in set.\n- **Attract mode:** one AI match and a title card, not the seven-beat montage.\n- **Replays:** no highlight replays.\n- **Photo album:** postcards are framed cards, not re-rendered scenes.\n- **Dev panel:** tools and tuning sliders only, with no Voice Lab, jukebox, SFX board or rig viewer.\n- **Final specials:** Golden Glare, House Edge and Lucky Seven are in simplified form.\n- **Online:** the host applies each client's presses on arrival. The plan's claim-and-validate scheme is not built.\n- **Engine patches:** two of eight are in the engine. The rest are handled in game code, as recorded in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n\n## Sections\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 01:24:24\n- Source: Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball (Team Ninja / Tecmo, 2003)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports (2v2 beach volleyball), with a light life sim and minigames\n- Perspective: broadcast side-on court view with a Serve Cam toggle; three-quarter view for walkable places; isometric island map\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (two engine patches), plain JavaScript, Playwright 1.63.0, Node 24\n- Art direction: PS1-style pixel art, sunset palette\n- Animation: engine procedural poses and attack moves\n- Audio: all synthesized in code, including Animalese dialogue voices\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world session\n- Testing: the 95-check command described above\n- Research: engine docs, the AI Hub protocol and client; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: about 14 real game issues. The most serious: the slot return was 41%, and a Pool Hop slip never recovered.\n- Critical / game-breaking: 2. The Pool Hop slip, and time staying frozen after the dev panel or photo mode. Both are fixed and covered.\n- Most helpful: the headless full-match run, which exposed serve and planner faults.\n- Least helpful: screenshot checks of small glyph details, and fixed-wait key scripts that cannot hit timing windows.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the fixed-step clock and headless mode, which made whole matches testable in Node.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: scene switches run through a fade, so tests must wait longer. The pixel font lacks many symbols, so the game maps them. The swimsuit and hair options were not available.\n- Most important to build myself: the referee, the planner, the timing judge, the AI, the text box with voices, and the vacation rules.\n- Hardest: making a ground-view match read as a side-on broadcast.\n- Engine changes: two marked `AOA:` (PlayStation symbols by default; a per-letter dialog voice hook that the game does not use).\n- Change one thing: a way to make scene changes immediate in headless tests.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the concrete numbers and the feature checklist.\n- Confusing: the plan and TASK.md disagreed on names and date; TASK.md was followed. The plan's scope is far larger than one session.\n- Hardest: keeping every system consistent at once. The engine-level swimsuit and motion-capture work was the hardest to justify.\n- Would change: ask for a priority order and a smaller first milestone, and state which parts may be simplified.\n\n## Next steps if you want to continue\n\nI'd pick the swimsuit art and the attract montage first, since they are the most visible gaps. The replays and the hub's claim-and-validate scheme come after that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":564740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"77311caf-5151-4024-bc4f-a574f824e56a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:00:54.500Z","request_id":"req_011CghccbfPGvvw2f3sehE3K"}
