{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghdNoN4Hyc3eDttJKLeh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Replays now show up in the simulated matches, and I replaced a placeholder check that was always true with a real one. Next I'll bring the About data, the dev notes and the engine record up to date with what was built, then regenerate the exit interview."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1554,"cache_read_input_tokens":660640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1554},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"21b0d896-f521-4685-8afc-cbe976b44232","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:10:45.289Z","request_id":"req_011CghdNnzza4QV65kr6qR7x"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghdNoN4Hyc3eDttJKLeh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ppPmXRkeSUdFfMBNDUiQK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > .tmp-doc.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst edit = (f, a, b) => { let s = fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8'); if (s.split(a).length !== 2) throw new Error(f + ' :: ' + a.slice(0, 80)); s = s.replace(a, () => b); fs.writeFileSync(f, s); };\nconst A = 'src/55-about.js';\nedit(A, \"    animation: 'The engine\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves (overhead, idles, cheers). No motion-capture clips were cut.',\",\n\"    animation: 'The engine\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves, plus 20 motion-capture clips cut from the engine\\\\'s three libraries (CC0 and CMU) for celebrations, dives, idles and the title; two-bone arm IK puts the hands on the ball for bumps, sets, spikes and serves.',\");\nedit(A, \"    'About 14 game issues: the slot return was 41% (fixed to about 91%);\", \"    'About 16 game issues: the slot return was 41% (fixed to about 91%);\");\nedit(A, \"keycap labels were unreadable; character cards overflowed; the location maps had uneven rows; a song name was unknown to the engine.',\",\n\"keycap labels were unreadable; character cards overflowed; the location maps had uneven rows; a song name was unknown to the engine; the dev panel and photo mode froze the screen black (the freeze ran during the fade-in, which a screenshot showed); the AI Hub copy referenced an undefined variable (the harness caught it).',\");\nedit(A, \"    'Two were game-breaking:\", \"    'Two were game-breaking:\");\nedit(A, \"    'Yes. Scene changes run through a fade, so a scene is entered a fraction of a second after game.go; tests had to wait longer than expected. The pixel font lacks many symbols (middle dot, the controller symbols, accented letters), so the game maps them before drawing. I also guessed at the overlay order and the Humanoid options: the suits can only be colours because the swimsuit and hair-style patches were not made.',\",\n\"    'Yes. Scene changes run through a fade, so a scene is entered a fraction of a second after game.go, and the fade runs on game time (so a freeze set at entry stalls it). The pixel font lacks many symbols (middle dot, the controller symbols, accented letters), so the game maps them before drawing. The swimsuit cuts and patterns are drawn over the rig, because the Humanoid has no swimsuit outfit; the rig\\\\'s arms take an IK target through solvePose, which worked without an engine change.',\");\nedit(A, \"    'Two patches to the engine (marked AOA in engine/my-3d2dge.js): the button-symbol default is PlayStation, and the dialog calls a function voice for every letter. Touch controls are off in the game code, not in the engine. The game\\\\'s own text box does the voices, so the dialog patch is present but not used.',\",\n\"    'Two patches to the engine (marked AOA in engine/my-3d2dge.js): the button-symbol default is PlayStation, and the dialog calls a function voice for every letter. Touch controls are off in the game code, not in the engine. The game\\\\'s own text box does the voices, so the dialog patch is present but not used. The motion-capture runtime (readable.js, mocap.js) and the clip set are separate files, loaded before the game.',\");\nconsole.log('ok');\nEOF\nnode .tmp-doc.mjs && rm .tmp-doc.mjs && cat > README-DEV.md <<'EOF'\n# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball: dev notes (built by claude-haiku-5-5, medium effort)\n\nThis folder is the dev folder. The deliverable is one level up:\n`../AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424.html`.\nThe exit interview is `../exit-interview.json` (written by `tools/exit.mjs` from `src/55-about.js`).\n\n## Commands\n- `node tools/build.mjs`: builds `build/game.js`, `build/dev.html` and the deliverable.\n- `node test/run.mjs`: the whole test command; prints only failures and one count line.\n  Flags: `--only=a,b` (core, data, ball, match, vacation, casino, story, ui, game, poolhop, playthrough, browser, hub),\n  `--skip-browser`, `--skip-hub`.\n- `node tools/browser-check.mjs`: the deliverable from file://, through the title, Beach Match and the pause menu.\n- `node tools/hub-check.mjs [players] [scenario] [latency jitter loss]`: one AI Hub harness run (standard, server, host-leave).\n- `node tools/shots.mjs`, `node tools/rigsheet.mjs`: review screenshots in test-output/.\n- `node tools/exit.mjs`: writes `exit-interview.json`.\n\n## Layout (src, concatenated in name order inside one IIFE)\n00 core, 01 tuning, 02 cast, 03 items, 04 world, 05 dialogue, 06 songs, 10 input and prompts, 11 UI kit, 11b text box,\n12 sound and Animalese, 13 rigs, 14 beach court, 15 motion capture and arm IK, 16 swimsuits and extra hair, 20 ball,\n21 match and referee, 22 players and judge, 23 AI, 24 match loop, 25 AI Hub session (claims and snapshots), 26 match scene,\n27 commentary, hints and the final's specials, 28 highlight replays, 30 vacation, 31 island map, 32 walkable places,\n33 shops, wardrobe, journal, mail, 34 story, 40 Pool Hop, 41 casino, 42 photo, album and postcards, 50 title and menu,\n50b How to Play and About, 51 attract (a loop of match, seven montage beats and a title card), 52 Beach Match setup,\n53 dev panel (tools, vacation, presentation, tuning), 54 day end, endings, credits, results, 55 About data, 99 main.\n\nVendor: `vendor/mocap/readable.js`, `mocap.js` (the engine's motion runtime, unmodified) and `aoa-clips.js` (20 clips cut with\nthe engine's `tools/anim-set.mjs` from its Quaternius, Mesh2Motion and CMU sets). `vendor/aihub-session.js` and `hub/` are the\nAI Hub client and harness, unmodified.\n\n## Known gaps (built more simply than the plan, or not at all)\n- Swimsuits: cuts and patterns are drawn over the rig (sleeves of rash guards are not drawn). Hair: twin buns, a puff and a bun\n  are drawn; braid, bob and curly use the engine's nearest styles. Sun hat and visor shapes are the engine's.\n- Arm IK covers bumps, sets, spikes and serves; blocks and the high-five use the engine's poses.\n- Motion capture plays on celebrations, the shrug after a lost point, dives and the title idles; not on every move.\n- Replays: three seconds at 0.4 speed with the serve camera; there are no separate camera cuts.\n- Attract: an AI match, the seven montage beats (each a short drawn scene with its caption, not footage) and a title card.\n- Photo album: thumbnails are live small renders of the saved fighter; a postcard re-renders one fighter. The R1 PNG export\n  saves the screen.\n- Dev panel: F1 reopens it once opened; the L3+R3 pad combo is not wired. The Voice Lab speaks one line per speaker.\n- Online: a client judges its own presses and sends a claim; the host validates the time window, the reach and that the touch\n  is still open. The host still runs the match.\n- Final specials: House Edge is one deep line shot per set; Lucky Seven forces a tape drop-over on Sonny's attack at game point;\n  the partner's cover rule for House Edge is not built.\n- Voices: dialogue only; no barks in matches.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && node tools/exit.mjs | tail -1 && timeout 900 node test/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Update About data and dev notes, regenerate the exit interview, run the full tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1554,"cache_read_input_tokens":660640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1554},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"9ea969ee-5246-4dc6-be47-5c337bd