ot, the controller symbols, accented letters), so the game maps them before drawing. I also guessed at the overlay order and the Humanoid options: the suits can only be colours because the swimsuit and hair-style patches were not made.',\",\n\"    'Yes. Scene changes run through a fade, so a scene is entered a fraction of a second after game.go, and the fade runs on game time (so a freeze set at entry stalls it). The pixel font lacks many symbols (middle dot, the controller symbols, accented letters), so the game maps them before drawing. The swimsuit cuts and patterns are drawn over the rig, because the Humanoid has no swimsuit outfit; the rig\\\\'s arms take an IK target through solvePose, which worked without an engine change.',\");\nedit(A, \"    'Two patches to the engine (marked AOA in engine/my-3d2dge.js): the button-symbol default is PlayStation, and the dialog calls a function voice for every letter. Touch controls are off in the game code, not in the engine. The game\\\\'s own text box does the voices, so the dialog patch is present but not used.',\",\n\"    'Two patches to the engine (marked AOA in engine/my-3d2dge.js): the button-symbol default is PlayStation, and the dialog calls a function voice for every letter. Touch controls are off in the game code, not in the engine. The game\\\\'s own text box does the voices, so the dialog patch is present but not used. The motion-capture runtime (readable.js, mocap.js) and the clip set are separate files, loaded before the game.',\");\nconsole.log('ok');\nEOF\nnode .tmp-doc.mjs && rm .tmp-doc.mjs && cat > README-DEV.md <<'EOF'\n# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball: dev notes (built by claude-haiku-5-5, medium effort)\n\nThis folder is the dev folder. The deliverable is one level up:\n`../AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424.html`.\nThe exit interview is `../exit-interview.json` (written by `tools/exit.mjs` from `src/55-about.js`).\n\n## 