{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghdV2WzmLoBeMoTmAspp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gaps the hook named are narrowed, but the goal is still not fully met. Several features are built in simpler form than the plan describes, so \"every feature implemented\" still doesn't hold. The deliverable and exit interview are in place, and all checks pass.\n\n## What changed this round\n\n- **Motion capture:** 20 clips cut from the engine's three libraries, using the engine's own tool. They play on point celebrations (each fighter's own), the shrug after a lost point, dives, and the title idles.\n- **Arm IK:** during a bump, set, spike or serve, both hands go to the ball, solved with the engine's two-bone IK.\n- **Swimsuits and hair:** each suit's cut and pattern is painted over the rig. Twin buns, a puff and a bun are drawn for the fighters who have them.\n- **Attract mode:** a loop of AI match, seven captioned montage beats, and a title card. Beats are short drawn scenes, not game footage.\n- **Replays:** after an ace, a stuffed block, or an eight-touch rally, the last 3 seconds replay at 0.4× with the serve camera.\n- **Dev panel:** added the Voice Lab, music jukebox, sound board and rig viewer, plus an F1 shortcut once it has been opened.\n- **Album:** saved postcards re-render live when opened, with live thumbnails in the grid and a PNG export on R1.\n- **Online:** clients judge their own presses on the hub clock and send claims. The host accepts a claim only inside the contact window, in reach, and while the touch is still open.\n- **Bugs fixed:** the dev panel and photo mode froze the screen black. The hub copy used an undefined variable, which the harness caught.\n\n## Verification\n\n`node test/run.mjs` runs 95 checks, all passing, in about 62 seconds. This includes the browser check of the file, and the four AI Hub harness scenarios.\n\nClaims are only exercised if the harness presses the right keys, so the claim path is not confirmed by the harness itself.\n\n## Still simplified or missing\n\n- Rash-guard sleeves, and the braid, bob, curly and sun-hat looks, are not drawn as the plan describes.\n- Motion capture covers celebrations, dives, idles and the title. It does not cover blocks or the high-five.\n- The montage is drawn scenes, not game footage.\n- The album shows one fighter per postcard, not group photos.\n- The dev panel has no F1 pad combo (L3+R3), and the Voice Lab speaks one line per speaker.\n- The host still runs the match. The plan's full claim scheme is only partly built.\n- House Edge is one deep line shot per set. The partner-cover rule is not built.\n- Voices cover dialogue only, with no barks during matches.\n\n## Sections\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-04 01:24:24\n- Source: Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball (Team Ninja / Tecmo, 2003)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: sports (2v2 beach volleyball), with a light life sim and minigames\n- Perspective: broadcast side-on court view with a Serve Cam toggle; three-quarter view for walkable places; isometric island map\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (two engine patches), plain JavaScript, the engine's motion runtime, Playwright 1.63.0, Node 24\n- Art direction: PS1-style pixel art, sunset palette, drawn swimsuits\n- Animation: engine rig poses and attack moves, 20 motion-capture clips, and arm IK\n- Audio: all synthesized in code, including Animalese dialogue voices\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world session, with client claims validated by the host\n- Testing: the 95-check command described above\n- Research: engine docs, the AI Hub protocol and client; no web research\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); headless Chromium\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n**Testing Feedback**\n- Issues caught: about 16 game issues. The most serious: the slot return was 41%, and a Pool Hop slip never recovered.\n- Critical / game-breaking: 2. The Pool Hop slip, and the black-screen freeze from the dev panel and photo mode. Both are fixed and covered.\n- Most helpful: the headless full-match run, which exposed serve and planner faults. The AI Hub harness also caught an undefined variable.\n- Least helpful: screenshot checks of small details, and fixed-wait key scripts, which cannot hit timing windows.\n\n**Engine Feedback**\n- Liked most: the fixed-step clock and headless mode, which made whole matches testable in Node. The motion runtime and two-bone IK were easy to attach to the rigs.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: the scene fade runs on game time, so a freeze set on entry stalls it. The pixel font lacks many symbols.\n- Most important to build myself: the referee, planner, timing judge, AI, text box with voices, and the vacation rules.\n- Hardest: making a ground-view match read as a side-on broadcast, and drawing swimsuits over a rig that has no swimsuit outfit.\n- Engine changes: two marked `AOA:` (PlayStation symbols by default; a per-letter dialog voice hook the game doesn't use). The swimsuits and arm IK are game code.\n- Change one thing: a way to make scene changes immediate in headless tests.\n\n**Prompt Feedback**\n- Liked most: the concrete numbers and the feature checklist, which made each gap easy to check.\n- Confusing: the plan and TASK.md disagreed on names and date; TASK.md was followed. The plan's scope is far larger than one session.\n- Hardest: keeping every system consistent at once, and the engine-level swimsuit and motion work.\n- Would change: ask for a priority order and a smaller first milestone, and state which parts may be simplified.\n\nThe exit interview is `exit-interview.json` in the work folder. It parses and fills every field.\n\nShould I keep going on the remaining simplified items, starting with blocks and the high-five clip, the group photo, and the full House Edge rule?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":666313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"44a5ca5d-59d9-4b0b-aabc-3818f4e5369a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:12:15.149Z","request_id":"req_011CghdV29RdaCnEpgFSLvUr"}
