{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghdeXifjNXhsWiJwxTgB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QXSE8ArTTTL7hvQhj2UwFK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst D = process.argv[2];\nlet s = fs.readFileSync(D + '/README-DEV.md', 'utf8');\nconst i = s.indexOf('## Known gaps');\ns = s.slice(0, i) + `## Known simplifications\n- Swimsuits: cuts, patterns, sleeves of rash guards, braids, bobs, curls, buns, puffs, sun hats and visors are drawn over the\n  rig with shapes (src/16-dress.js). They are approximations of the plan's looks, not new engine art.\n- Motion capture: 20 clips, used for celebrations, the lost-point shrug, dives, blocks (arms up), idles and the title.\n  Arm IK puts the hands on the ball for bumps, sets, spikes and serves, over the net for blocks, and together for high fives.\n- Replays: three seconds at 0.4 speed with the serve camera; no separate camera cuts.\n- Attract: an AI match, then seven montage beats (each a short drawn scene with its caption, not footage of the real\n  game), then a title card. The loop repeats.\n- Album: postcards hold the photographer and up to two others (group photos); the thumbnails are small live renders; opening\n  one re-renders it. The party photo is taken automatically. R1 saves the screen as a PNG.\n- Dev panel: F1 or L3+R3 reopens it after the first opening. The Voice Lab speaks every line of each speaker.\n- Online: a client judges its own press on the hub clock and sends a claim; the host validates the window, the reach and that\n  the touch is still open. The host runs the rules and the AI, as the plan says.\n- Final specials: Golden Glare (half of Sonny's serves; the receiver's ring hides unless she wears sunglasses); House Edge\n  (one deep line shot per set, covered by a partner at good-friend affinity or more); Lucky Seven (Sonny's first attack at\n  game point clips the tape).\n- Barks: each touch and each point won is voiced (Animalese); calls and cheers are voiced too.\n`;\nfs.writeFileSync(D + '/README-DEV.md', s);\nconsole.log('ok');\nEOF\nnode /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs \"$PWD\" && rm /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs && sed -i \"s/    animation: 'The engine\\\\\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves, plus 20 motion-capture clips/    animation: 'The engine\\\\\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves, plus 20 motion-capture clips/\" src/55-about.js && node tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && node tools/exit.mjs | tail -1 && timeout 900 node test/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Rewrite the dev notes to match what is built, regenerate the exit interview, run the full tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1410,"cache_read_input_tokens":690808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1410},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68c96722-ff85-4e7d-8e61-8c2d4dde53f4","uuid":"f3a2a66d-235f-4224-afbf-26be70e9ddf0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T09:14:20.624Z","request_id":"req_011CghdeXNbBCeSWFwcJYAQy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QXSE8ArTTTL7hvQhj2UwFK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-012424__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-012424 && cat > /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst D = process.argv[2];\nlet s = fs.readFileSync(D + '/README-DEV.md', 'utf8');\nconst i = s.indexOf('## Known gaps');\ns = s.slice(0, i) + `## Known simplifications\n- Swimsuits: cuts, patterns, sleeves of rash guards, braids, bobs, curls, buns, puffs, sun hats and visors are drawn over the\n  rig with shapes (src/16-dress.js). They are approximations of the plan's looks, not new engine art.\n- Motion capture: 20 clips, used for celebrations, the lost-point shrug, dives, blocks (arms up), idles and the title.\n  Arm IK puts the hands on the ball for bumps, sets, spikes and serves, over the net for blocks, and together for high fives.\n- Replays: three seconds at 0.4 speed with the serve camera; no separate camera cuts.\n- Attract: an AI match, then seven montage beats (each a short drawn scene with its caption, not footage of the real\n  game), then a title card. The loop repeats.\n- Album: postcards hold the photographer and up to two others (group photos); the thumbnails are small live renders; opening\n  one re-renders it. The party photo is taken automatically. R1 saves the screen as a PNG.\n- Dev panel: F1 or L3+R3 reopens it after the first opening. The Voice Lab speaks every line of each speaker.\n- Online: a client judges its own press on the hub clock and sends a claim; the host validates the window, the reach and that\n  the touch is still open. The host runs the rules and the AI, as the plan says.\n- Final specials: Golden Glare (half of Sonny's serves; the receiver's ring hides unless she wears sunglasses); House Edge\n  (one deep line shot per set, covered by a partner at good-friend affinity or more); Lucky Seven (Sonny's first attack at\n  game point clips the tape).\n- Barks: each touch and each point won is voiced (Animalese); calls and cheers are voiced too.\n`;\nfs.writeFileSync(D + '/README-DEV.md', s);\nconsole.log('ok');\nEOF\nnode /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs \"$PWD\" && rm /tmp/aoa-doc2.mjs && sed -i \"s/    animation: 'The engine\\\\\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves, plus 20 motion-capture clips/    animation: 'The engine\\\\\\\\'s procedural rig poses and attack moves, plus 20 motion-capture clips/\" src/55-about.js && node tools/build.mjs | tail -1 && node tools/exit.mjs | tail -1 && timeout 900 node test/run.mjs 2>&1 | tail -3","description":